0:15:00.000Z","notes":"Tamchy / Ysyk-Kul (UCFL/IKU), USD. New record, 18 Nov 2026. Single source: FCG OPS quote 129033 (17 Nov 2026; A6-AFO E35L 24.3 t, arrival from UCFM 23 Nov 05:45 UTC and departure to OMDW 09:10 UTC, 4 pax each way, 3,176.74 EUR). The 20 lines reconcile to the cent and confirm FCG disbursement 11% on everything except supervision (2,411.48 x 11% = 265.26). Quoted in EUR at 1 EUR = 1.0673 USD, the same rate as the FCG UCFM quote of the same day; the airport items converted at that rate recover the Kyrgyz USD tariff: landing 18 + 2% = 18.36 per ton, terminal navigation 6.12 per ton, en-route 45.90 per 100 km, follow-me 21.42, GPU 48.96 per 15 min, airport ramp 399.84 + marshalling 18.36 = handling 418.20, departing pax 13.46 + 11.02 + 20.41 = 44.88. FCG's own fees are in EUR and converted at the panel rate 1.1215: supervision 500 EUR = 560.75. FCG rounds MTOW up to whole tons (CL60 22, E35L 25, GLF4 34, GL5T 44, GLEX 46, GL7T 53); landing, parking, flight safety, navigation and both night rows are entered on that. Parking 15% of landing per started day, first 3 h free (quote says 3:15, safe side). Aircraft security 33% of landing per started day. Navigation row = en-route 45.90 (one 100 km unit on this short domestic leg) + 6.12 per ton + follow-me 21.42; the quote gives one en-route rate and no weight band, so GL7T may be understated. VIP lounge 116.28 per pax, both arrival and departure on this quote. Night surcharges from the quote's remarks: landing 9.5% per movement (Mar-Sep 19:30-06:00 LT, Oct-Feb 18:00-07:30 LT, 19% if both movements fall in the period) and terminal navigation 20% (22:00-06:00 LT); in the panel on the safe side all year 18:00-08:00 and 22:00-06:00. Landing permit: only a 50% surcharge for an urgent request or correction is quoted, no base price, row left empty. Children 2-12 pay 50% of passenger handling and terminal charges, under 2 exempt. The quote's 'Other Services 2% sales tax' line of 5.31 EUR could not be traced to the items it is levied on, so no row was opened. The GPU row is per hour while the quote charged 15 min. Handling 418.20 entered in all groups: the quote prices ramp charge and marshalling per occurrence with no weight band. Service list copied from UCFM by user decision so that further handlers drop straight in; everything else comes from this quote only. Time zone Asia/Bishkek set on 19 Nov 2026 so that the night surcharge rows work. K-GENERATION added as a second handler on 19 Nov 2026 from three documents for the same flight (T7-KBI CL60 21.863 t, UCFM-UCFL-OMDB, 19 Feb 2026, arrival 07:44 departure 10:25, 2 passengers), confirmed by the user as UCFL: airport act AUP02300 of 19 Feb 2026, airport invoice AUP00455 of the same date, and K-Generation invoice 9207 of 04 Mar 2026. The chain reconciles to the cent: the act's nine lines total 1,030.00 (90,073.50 KGS at 87.45), plus 2 per cent sales tax 1,050.60; the airport invoice adds the VIP lounge 91.20 and an agency service 350.00 with 12 per cent VAT and 2 per cent sales tax, 399.00, giving 1,540.80; K-Generation then bills handling 1,449.60 (1,050.60 + 399.00), passenger handling 91.20, catering 630.42, disbursement 130.27, supervision 200.00 and catering arrangement 50.00, total 2,551.49. The disbursement is exactly 6 per cent of handling plus passenger handling plus catering, which matches the 6 per cent carried for this handler at UCFM; supervision and the catering arrangement stay outside the base. Airport lines are entered gross, including the 2 per cent sales tax, the same convention as K-Generation at UCFM: landing 21.863 t x 18.00 = 394.00 becomes 401.88, flight safety 33 per cent of landing becomes 132.60, the departing passenger charges (servicing 13.20, terminal use 10.80, electronic check-in 2.40, airport dues 20.00 = 46.40) become 47.33 per pax, individual transport for crew 45.00 becomes 45.90, and aircraft receiving and its departure 18.00 becomes 18.36 in the Handling Fee row. Agency services 399.00 is entered with the VAT and sales tax included, since that is the amount K-Generation passes on. The VIP lounge 91.20 for 2 passengers is 45.60 per passenger; the invoice does not say which direction, so it is entered on departure. The act's apron service 350.00 is carried inside the Handling Fee row by user decision of 19 Nov 2026: 357.00 gross with the 2 per cent sales tax, on top of the 18.36 aircraft receiving, so the row is 375.36 and the panel matches this invoice for the same flight. Only the CL60 group is filled; the documents cover one aircraft and the other groups stay empty until a further document. Catering and the catering arrangement fee are not entered, as at every other airport. No parking was charged for the 2 h 41 min on the ground.","tz":"Asia/Bishkek"}},"base":{"UCFL":["2026-11-19T07:20:00.000Z"]},"settings":{"fuel":{"price":1111,"updatedAt":"2026-10-28T13:11:12.679Z"},"fx":{"rates":{"AED":0.272294,"BHD":2.659574,"CHF":1.2141,"EGP":0.01806,"EUR":1.1215,"GBP":1.3347,"ILS":0.3218,"JPY":0.006324,"KWD":3.2284,"PLN":0.2562,"QAR":0.274725,"SAR":0.266667,"TRY":0.02017},"source":"ECB referans kurları 20 Eki 2026 (EUR çaprazı); SAR, BHD, AED, QAR dolara sabit; KWD XE 20 Eki 2026 23:00 UTC; EGP 55.37 per USD (Egyptian Streets, 22 Oct 2026 close)","updatedAt":"2026-10-20T14:00:00.000Z"}}}